> Of course it does (at least, wizard mode does).
> 
> Start with the ^O command: this tells you at what level Sokoban starts.
> Next, ^V: go to that level.
> Next, ^F: magic mapping.
> Next, ^T: teleport to the stairs.
> [ Go up the stairs.
> You took the wrong upstairs.
> Go back down.
> ^T to the other upstairs. ]
> Go up the stairs.
> Do Sokoban.
> 
> The intermezzo between square brackets is optional.  :-)

Or, to avoid the intermezzo altogether, follow the rather simpler
procedure:

First, ^V ? to get a level-teleport menu.
Choose soko4.
Do Sokoban.

(You may also find it helpful to set the SPLEVTYPE environment
variable to force the Sokoban levels to be a particular variant, to
save repetition.)

